---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: The Interdependency WebMCP
description: Live browser-native WebMCP and remote MCP access to the commit-pinned The Interdependency skill registry.
permalink: /webmcp/
webmcp: true
---
<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="webmcp-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">WebMCP Challenge · live public surface</p>
  <h1 id="webmcp-title">The Interdependency WebMCP</h1>
  <p><strong>The page is the provider.</strong> Human and agent use the same commit-pinned skill material. A human chooses the skill; the page records that exact selection for the browser agent; the agent can then use the selected canonical skill with its authorized tools to deliver the requested change.</p>
  <p><strong>Remote MCP:</strong> <code>https://the-interdependency-mcp.onrender.com/mcp</code></p>
  <p><a href="https://the-interdependency-mcp.onrender.com/health">Open remote MCP health check</a></p>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="webmcp-status-title">
  <h2 id="webmcp-status-title">LIVE</h2>
  <p data-webmcp-status data-state="hmmm">Loading the commit-pinned registry and checking browser WebMCP support…</p>
  <p data-remote-mcp-status data-state="hmmm">Checking remote MCP health…</p>
  <p><strong>Registry source:</strong> <span data-webmcp-source>resolving…</span></p>
  <noscript><p>JavaScript is disabled, so browser WebMCP registration and selection handoff cannot run. The human-readable catalogue remains available, and the remote MCP endpoint remains independent.</p></noscript>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="skill-catalog-title">
  <p class="eyebrow">Human selection surface</p>
  <h2 id="skill-catalog-title">Choose the skill the agent should use</h2>
  <p>The public human catalogue is deliberately narrow: msdmd and its metadata-block applications first, followed by the METAPAT meta skill. The rest of <code>skill-lib</code> remains canonical in its source repository but is not presented as a human choice here.</p>

  <form data-human-skill-filter-form>
    <label for="human-skill-filter">Search presented skills</label>
    <input id="human-skill-filter" data-human-skill-filter name="skill-filter" type="search" placeholder="documentation, capabilities, boundaries, meta…" autocomplete="off">
    <span aria-live="polite" data-human-skill-count>Presented skills shown</span>
  </form>

  <h3>msdmd skills</h3>
  <div class="grid" data-human-skill-catalog data-skill-group="msdmd">
    {% for skill in generated.skillRegistry.skills %}
    {% if skill.kind == "metadata-block" %}
    <article class="card" data-human-skill data-skill-name="{{ skill.name }}" data-skill-kind="{{ skill.kind }}">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ skill.kind }}</p>
      <h4>{{ skill.name | replace("-", " ") }}</h4>
      <p><code>{{ skill.name }}</code></p>
      <details data-skill-description>
        <summary>Description</summary>
        <p>{{ skill.description }}</p>
      </details>
      {% if skill.depends_on and skill.depends_on.length %}
      <p><strong>Depends on:</strong> {% for dependency in skill.depends_on %}<code>{{ dependency }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
      {% else %}
      <p><strong>Depends on:</strong> none declared</p>
      {% endif %}
      <p><button type="button" data-select-skill aria-pressed="false">Select this skill</button></p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/{{ generated.skillRegistry.source.repository }}/blob/{{ generated.skillRegistry.source.commit }}/{{ skill.path }}">Read canonical SKILL.md</a></p>
    </article>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <h3>meta skills</h3>
  <div class="grid" data-human-skill-catalog data-skill-group="meta">
    {% for skill in generated.skillRegistry.skills %}
    {% if skill.name == "meta" %}
    <article class="card" data-human-skill data-skill-name="{{ skill.name }}" data-skill-kind="{{ skill.kind }}">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ skill.kind }}</p>
      <h4>{{ skill.name | replace("-", " ") }}</h4>
      <p><code>{{ skill.name }}</code></p>
      <details data-skill-description>
        <summary>Description</summary>
        <p>{{ skill.description }}</p>
      </details>
      {% if skill.depends_on and skill.depends_on.length %}
      <p><strong>Depends on:</strong> {% for dependency in skill.depends_on %}<code>{{ dependency }}</code>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}</p>
      {% else %}
      <p><strong>Depends on:</strong> none declared</p>
      {% endif %}
      <p><button type="button" data-select-skill aria-pressed="false">Select this skill</button></p>
      <p><a href="https://github.com/{{ generated.skillRegistry.source.repository }}/blob/{{ generated.skillRegistry.source.commit }}/{{ skill.path }}">Read canonical SKILL.md</a></p>
    </article>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="hmmm-boundary" data-selected-skill-boundary>
    <strong>Selected skill</strong>
    <span data-selected-skill>No skill selected. Choose a card above; selection will be written into this page's URL and agent-visible state.</span>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="webmcp-tools-title">
  <h2 id="webmcp-tools-title">Agent view of the same material</h2>
  <p>Selection does not itself mutate a repository. It identifies the exact skill the agent should load and use. Selecting a card automatically opens its description, fills the inspect and closure inputs, and publishes the same registry record below for agent handoff.</p>

  <p>
    <button type="button" data-webmcp-action="status">STATUS</button>
    <button type="button" data-webmcp-action="list">LIST</button>
  </p>

  <form data-webmcp-find>
    <label for="webmcp-find-query">FIND</label>
    <input id="webmcp-find-query" name="query" type="text" value="metadata" required>
    <button type="submit">Find skill</button>
  </form>

  <form data-webmcp-inspect>
    <label for="webmcp-inspect-name">INSPECT</label>
    <input id="webmcp-inspect-name" name="name" type="text" value="msdmd" required>
    <button type="submit">Inspect skill</button>
  </form>

  <form data-webmcp-closure>
    <label for="webmcp-closure-name">RESOLVE CLOSURE</label>
    <input id="webmcp-closure-name" name="name" type="text" value="msdmd" required>
    <button type="submit">Resolve closure</button>
  </form>

  <pre tabindex="0" data-webmcp-output>Select a skill above, or choose STATUS, LIST, FIND, INSPECT, or RESOLVE CLOSURE.</pre>
</section>

<section class="panel" aria-labelledby="webmcp-boundary-title">
  <h2 id="webmcp-boundary-title">One source, one selection, multiple delivery surfaces</h2>
  <pre tabindex="0">skill-lib/SKILL.md + skills.json
        ↓ commit-pinned projection
human-readable card ↔ selected skill ↔ agent-visible page state
                                    ↓
                         browser WebMCP / remote MCP
                                    ↓
                     agent's authorized change tools</pre>
  <p>The website does not gain repository-write authority merely because a skill was selected. The selected skill constrains how the agent should work; any actual change still occurs through the agent's separately authorized tool boundary. <code>The-Interdependency/skill-lib</code> remains authority for the skill itself.</p>
</section>

<div class="hmmm-boundary"><strong>hmmm</strong><span>Selection is instruction, not permission. A useful skill can tell an agent how to change something without quietly granting it the authority to change everything.</span></div>
